ria\n43\t\n44\t- The guardrails integration is enabled on a GA distribution without any experimental flag or TP opt-in gate.\n45\t- Validation evidence exists that the integration works against the GA distribution's safety-provider surface.\n46\t- The integration is documented as a supported configuration, with the documentation reviewed by the Llama Stack owning team.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- **HLR-4 (P1)** — full coverage: safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9173457229f239ec","agent_id":"ae4b94e893fe1c855","session_id":"514c5544-223d-42a7-ba52-fa0d432c2321","uuid":"871655be-8576-4586-8d1f-7342ae960f81","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:53:25.237Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9005497a9ab2f444","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
