{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb4166a99668f8ca","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment and gap inventory\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment and gap inventory\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's central unknown: no systematic GA-readiness assessment of Llama Stack has been done, and TP feedback is scattered across support tickets. This investigation inventories the gaps between current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling, and produces the definitive GA scope that sizes and shapes the downstream stability, hardening, and support-posture work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Aggregate and triage TP feedback from the existing support-ticket record.\n34\t- Assess current Llama Stack quality against the GA-bar dimensions named in the strategy: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling.\n35\t- Produce a ranked gap inventory in which every gap is traced to evidence (ticket, repo finding, or test result) and classified by severity and whether it blocks GA.\n36\t- Recommend the definitive GA scope: which gaps must close before GA, which are deferred, and what each implies for the API stability/hardening work and the production support posture.\n37\t- Verify scale-limit findings against a live cluster where local inspection cannot answer them.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A gap inventory document exists covering all four GA-bar dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap traced to evidence.\n42\t- Every gap carries a severity rating and a GA-blocker / deferrable classification.\n43\t- A recommended GA scope is produced from the inventory, sufficient for the downstream stability/hardening and support-posture work to be sized directly from it without re-deriving the analysis.\n44\t- The GA scope recommendation is submitted to the strategy stakeholders for ratification.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — full coverage: this epic is the GA-readiness assessment that inventories the gaps between TP quality and the GA bar and produces the definitive GA scope.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a22b8b682f5ae2a","agent_id":"ab364ff8202a904a1","session_id":"514c5544-223d-42a7-ba52-fa0d432c2321","uuid":"6f2e7be3-90b1-4c61-9918-ccaa47168f32","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:54:30.765Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb4166a99668f8ca","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
