{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4166170fed3e7ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Publish Llama Stack API stability guarantee and close GA-bar gaps\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds materially different gap\n15\t    severity or scope, rewrite this epic's remediation items from the ratified inventory\n16\t    before implementation; the API versioning, deprecation policy, and two-release\n17\t    upgrade-path testing proceed unchanged.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Publish Llama Stack API stability guarantee and close GA-bar gaps\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDelivers the API stability guarantee for the published Llama Stack surface — versioned APIs, a deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases — and closes the GA-blocker quality gaps (error handling, scale limits, and related findings) identified by the GA-readiness assessment. This is the core engineering work that moves Llama Stack from Tech Preview quality to the GA bar.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Version the published API surface and publish a deprecation policy for it.\n44\t- Implement and test the upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases.\n45\t- Remediate the GA-blocker gaps in the assessment's inventory that fall on the API surface (error handling, scale limits, and other assessed findings), staying within GA-bar quality work — new feature development is out of scope for this strategy.\n46\t- Record any assessment findings that amount to new feature work as strategy feedback rather than absorbing them here.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The published API surface is versioned and carries a written deprecation policy.\n51\t- The upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases is tested and the test evidence exists.\n52\t- Every GA-blocker gap the assessment assigned to API stability, error handling, or scale limits is either remediated or explicitly deferred with rationale in the ratified GA scope.\n53\t- The GA-bar quality work is limited to the assessed gap inventory; no new-feature scope has been added.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — full coverage: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases.\n58\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — downstream consumption: remediates the GA-blocker gaps this epic's assessment inventory identifies (the assessment itself is tracked separately).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability note\n61\t\n62\tThis epic's scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; its remediation items are sized from that inventory. See the decomposition summary's Health Warnings for the re-split trigger if the scoped hardening exceeds the epic guideline.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a22b8b682f5ae2a","agent_id":"ab364ff8202a904a1","session_id":"514c5544-223d-42a7-ba52-fa0d432c2321","uuid":"4fa48a96-66cf-48d7-8047-e91393bca3b9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:54:31.376Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4166170fed3e7ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
